n, considering cases where a vertex *v* is not in the 1-ball and its function value is not 1. If the function value is 0, a contradiction is reached using the dominating function property.\\n\\nIf the function value is 2, a contradiction arises from the uniqueness of the vertex *u* with value 2. Finally, a set cardinality is shown by deriving from a valid inequality.\\n\\n\\n**Deriving an upper bound**\\n\\nEstablish an upper bound for the cardinality of the 1-ball centered at *u* within graph *G* by observing it is a subset of the universal set of vertices. The proof then focuses on the relationship between Roman weight, and the cardinality of vertices with function value 1.\\n\\nThe cardinality of vertices with value 1 plus 2 is less than or equal to the Roman weight. This is derived by using a set subset and the properties of the Roman weight function, and ensuring the special vertex *u* isn't counted in the sum of ones. This then leads to the final inequality.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"cat << 'EOF' > test_unique_two.lean\\\\nimport Mathlib\\\\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\\\\n\\\\nopen SimpleGraph\\\\nopen GraphCalc\\\\n\\\\nlemma minUpTo_le {n : ℕ} {p : ℕ → Prop} [DecidablePred p] (k : ℕ) (hk : k ≤ n) (hp : p k) :\\\\n    minUpTo n p ≤ k := by\\\\n  unfold minUpTo\\\\n  have hmem : k ∈ (Finset.range (n + 1)).filter p := by\\\\n    rw [Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_range]\\\\n    exact ⟨Nat.lt_succ_of_le hk, hp⟩\\\\n  have hmin := Finset.min_le hmem\\\\n  generalize hmin_eq : ((Finset.range (n + 1)).filter p).min = m\\\\n  rw [hmin_eq] at hmin\\\\n  cases m with\\\\n  | top => contradiction\\\\n  | coe val =>\\\\n    simp only [WithTop.coe_le_coe] at hmin\\\\n    exact hmin\\\\n\\\\ntheorem radius_le_eccentricity {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V) :\\\\n    GraphCalc.radius G ≤ GraphCalc.eccentricity G v := by\\\\n  unfold GraphCalc.radius\\\\n  have hmem : GraphCalc.eccentricity G v ∈ Finset.image (GraphCalc.eccentricity G) Finset.univ := by\\\\n    apply Finset.mem_image_of_mem\\\\n    exact Finset.mem_univ v\\\\n  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := Finset.min_of_mem hmem\\\\n  rw [hb]\\\\n  have hle : (Finset.image (GraphCalc.eccentricity G) Finset.univ).min ≤ ↑(GraphCalc.eccentricity G v) :=\\\\n    Finset.min_le hmem\\\\n  rw [hb] at hle\\\\n  exact WithTop.coe_le_coe.mp hle\\\\n\\\\nlemma mem_ballWithin_of_walk {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] {v w : V} (p : G.Walk v w) :\\\\n    w ∈ ballWithin G p.length v := by\\\\n  induction p using SimpleGraph.Walk.concatRec with\\\\n  | Hnil =>\\\\n    dsimp [ballWithin]\\\\n    exact Finset.mem_singleton_self _\\\\n  | Hconcat p hadj ih =>\\\\n    rw [SimpleGraph.Walk.length_concat]\\\\n    dsimp [ballWithin]\\\\n    rw [Finset.mem_union]\\\\n    right\\\\n    rw [Finset.mem_biUnion]\\\\n    refine ⟨_, ih, ?_⟩\\\\n    rw [Finset.mem_filter]\\\\n    exact ⟨Finset.mem_univ _, hadj⟩\\\\n\\\\nlemma mem_ballWithin_one_of_adj {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (c u : V) (hadj : G.Adj c u) :\\\\n    u ∈ ballWi\\n<truncated 11861 bytes>\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking test_unique_two.lean\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check test_unique_two.lean with check.sh\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\r\n\n"}
